WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.339
Switch tabs mid-ride, and Telo Ride keeps the true time. Come back ten minutes

00:00:07.339 --> 00:00:09.530
later, and nothing has drifted.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.219
A hidden tab's timers run once a minute. The bike keeps talking, and the ride keeps

00:00:15.219 --> 00:00:16.345
its own clock.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.012
Shown again, the race is at ten ten, in the second recovery, with the distance a

00:00:28.012 --> 00:00:29.688
visible tab would show.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:40.823
A class ride does the same: the clock and the segment are exactly where they should

00:00:40.823 --> 00:00:41.293
be.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:53.605
And a running race now asks before the tab closes, as a class already did.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:05.752
The race after ten hidden minutes, from a phone to the full screen.

00:01:14.847 --> 00:01:19.212
What the tests prove: ten throttled minutes, and the clock, segment and distance

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:20.058
stay true.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:29.774
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:34.631
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:34.631 --> 00:01:36.302
every hill and interval.

00:01:36.647 --> 00:01:41.825
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:41.825 --> 00:01:47.273
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:50.263
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:50.608 --> 00:01:53.101
A custom workout lives under Profile.
